From 630b9428bfe023aad306ec6e480c6b954843e3cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 18:19:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] wip/kv-residency B2: a STREAMING KV takes the sparse QSA
 decode arm (+34/+47 %)

A windowed KV (block 15) keeps only its newest W cells in VRAM; the tail
lives in pinned host RAM, so a spilled read costs bytes/55.7 GB/s instead
of bytes/565 GB/s.  The dense decode arm reads the whole used extent every
step, so on a streaming cache it is the wrong arm -- but qwen4exp's arch
policy only knew DEPTH (qsa_dense_decode_until = 1<<62 on gfx1201), never
the cache's placement.

  llama_kv_cache::is_streaming(n_kv)  (and the context accessor) answers
  'a window is active and the used extent has passed it', and
  qwen4exp_kv_streams() skips the dense decode arm when it holds.

Measured (Flash-Next GSQ-IQ3_XXS, -ncmoe 48, q8_0, 1 GPU, -n 400,
-ot per_layer_token_embd.*=CPU -lm none -lzm off, 2 reps, +-0.2 %):
  depth     resident+dense   streamed+dense   streamed+B2(default sparse)
  102 899      42.16          23.42 / 23.54      31.43 / 31.46  (+34.3 %)
  180 035      37.10          16.51 / 16.50      24.31 / 24.29  (+47.3 %)
Arena on the streamed arms: 25 338.3 MiB / 61.9 % vs 23 580 / 57.6 %
(103k) and 22 701 / 55.5 % (180k).

Text: resident default == resident flag-off (853 chars 77a40bf40be1, so
the change is inert on a resident cache); streamed default == streamed
forced-sparse (1159, e6080aaf2318, so the default IS the sparse arm);
streamed dense differs (1158, 0f1ad14496c9 -- a documented regime change,
GREEDY-PURITY.md 45/63).  Prefill is untouched (always QSA).

LLAMA_QSA_DENSE_DECODE_STREAM=0 restores the pre-B2 behaviour.
Campaign branch only.
---
 src/llama-kv-cache.cpp  | 11 +++++++++++
 src/llama-kv-cache.h    | 10 ++++++++++
 src/models/qwen4exp.cpp | 33 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 3 files changed, 53 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
index 5aefac9f8..b99688d04 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -1961,6 +1961,17 @@ bool llama_kv_cache::get_can_shift() const {
     return true;
 }
 
+bool llama_kv_cache::is_streaming(uint32_t n_kv) const {
+    // The window is a CELL count and it is only ever set when the region provider is in use; a cell at or
+    // above it is backed by pinned host RAM (the slide is monotone).  `n_kv` is the extent the graph is
+    // about to read, so this answers the question the arm choice actually asks.
+    return kv_resident_cells != 0 && n_kv > kv_resident_cells;
+}
+
+bool llama_kv_cache_context::is_streaming(uint32_t n_kv) const {
+    return kv->is_streaming(n_kv);
+}
+
 uint32_t llama_kv_cache::get_size() const {
     const auto & cells = v_cells[seq_to_stream[0]];
 
